{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310643,"nonce":"2E3cpuuc+Ij4mBCcep5/YhJbjUA=","title":"FIXED ffda0925: a parameter assigned in a loop body got no loop-carried phi (the type lookup read func.locals only, which parameters never ...","message":"```haxe\nstatic function build(head:Node):Node {\n    for (i in 0...3) { var n = new Node(i); n.next = head; head = n; }\n    return head;            // W0020 \"Return value IrId(17) not found\" -\u003e trap stub -\u003e SIGILL\n}\n```\n`lower_while_loop`'s `loop_var_initial_values` gate (stmt/loops.rs) looked the initial\ntype up in `func.locals` ONLY. Parameters are seeded into `register_types`\n(ir/functions.rs) and bound into `symbol_map` (mir/expr/functions.rs\nlower_function_body) and are NEVER registered as locals — so the symbol was dropped\nbefore any phi existed, the post-loop repoint never ran, and `return head` read the\nbody's register. The three for_in lowerers already had the `get_register_type`\nfallback; the two while lowerers did not.\n\n1. **`SymbolKind::Parameter` is never constructed** — zero assignment sites in the\n   whole repo; `create_variable_with_type` (tast/symbols.rs) hardcodes\n   `SymbolKind::Variable`. So `is_parameter_symbol` was ALWAYS FALSE and the filter\n   term guarded by \"function parameters are immutable\" was dead code. I \"fixed\" it\n   five times before noticing. The term is now DELETED.\n2. **`for (i in a...b)` NEVER reaches the for_in lowerers.** It desugars at TAST time\n   (ast_lowering/expr/loops.rs, the `BinaryOp::Range` branch) to `TypedStatement::For`\n   → `HirStatement::While` → `lower_while_loop`. So does the inline array-iterator\n   branch. `lower_for_in_*` runs only for Map iteration and the iterator protocol.\n   A path trace that prints no function name for lower_while_loop reads as \"stdlib\n   only\" — mine did, and I misdiagnosed from it.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_loop_assigned_parameter_no_phi` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}